{"q":"1071","t":"Greatest Common Divisor of Strings","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>For two strings <code>s</code> and <code>t</code>, we say &quot;<code>t</code> divides <code>s</code>&quot; if and only if <code>s = t + t + t + ... + t + t</code> (i.e., <code>t</code> is concatenated with itself one or more times).</p>\n\n<p>Given two strings <code>str1</code> and <code>str2</code>, return <em>the largest string </em><code>x</code><em> such that </em><code>x</code><em> divides both </em><code>str1</code><em> and </em><code>str2</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">str1 = &quot;ABCABC&quot;, str2 = &quot;ABC&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">&quot;ABC&quot;</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">str1 = &quot;ABABAB&quot;, str2 = &quot;ABAB&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">&quot;AB&quot;</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">str1 = &quot;LEET&quot;, str2 = &quot;CODE&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">&quot;&quot;</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 4:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">str1 = &quot;AAAAAB&quot;, str2 = &quot;AAA&quot;</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">&quot;&quot;</span>​​​​​​​</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= str1.length, str2.length &lt;= 1000</code></li>\n\t<li><code>str1</code> and <code>str2</code> consist of English uppercase letters.</li>\n</ul>\n","h":["The greatest common divisor must be a prefix of each string, so we can try all prefixes."],"m":"{\n  \"name\": \"gcdOfStrings\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"str1\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"str2\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"return\": {\n    \"type\": \"string\"\n  }\n}\n","g":[{"name":"Math","slug":"math"},{"name":"String","slug":"string"},{"name":"Euclidean Algorithm","slug":"euclidean-algorithm"},{"name":"Greatest Common Divisor","slug":"greatest-common-divisor"}],"s":[{"t":"Find Greatest Common Divisor of Array","s":"find-greatest-common-divisor-of-array","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Smallest Even Multiple","s":"smallest-even-multiple","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Find the Maximum Factor Score of Array","s":"find-the-maximum-factor-score-of-array","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Meta","facebook"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Oracle","oracle"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",3],["Microsoft","microsoft",2]],"b":[["Amazon","amazon",2]],"m":[["Meta","facebook",17],["TikTok","tiktok",7],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",6],["Oracle","oracle",2]]}}